{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398800-methuselah-s-thirst-from-age-or-generation","id":1398800,"title":"Methuselah's Thirst from age or generation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-25T09:21:37-07:00","id":1398800,"title":"Methuselah's Thirst from age or generation?","content":"I know that the Thirs of Ages is effecting low generation cainites and that people are fearing it, because it brings blood bonds with it and so the old want to avoid it feed from thin bloods or kill the cainite they are drinking from. But because it is not really a problem to those cainite couples who are blood bound to each other my question would be, would it possible for them, to embrace some of their servants so he drinks from mortals and so feed to his masters his vitae? Or would this not be possible because it is comming from generation and not from age?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T09:58:44-07:00","id":1398813,"title":"","content":"Methuselah's thirst only happens to those who are over a thousand yeas old that have also committed Diablerie to lower their generation, or committed Diablerie many times. It's why Helena has a drinking problem yet Critis does not. It's a self inflicted wound brought about by drinking peoples souls down is how I run it. Nasty even for vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T10:43:06-07:00","id":1398822,"title":"","content":"A little bit of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T11:17:47-07:00","id":1398826,"title":"","content":"As a digression, I've normally run it that you can't be Blood Bound to your own vitae. So you can drink freely from your childer without risking a Bond. Grandchilder etc. takes more drinks. It means that its practically possible for some kindred with Methuselahs Thirst and some humanity to exists, and gives a reason for the older kindred to sire occasionally and keep an eye on their offspring in case they need to pop out of torpor for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T12:07:09-07:00","id":1398841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398800-methuselah-s-thirst-from-age-or-generation#post1398800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that the Thirs of Ages is effecting low generation cainites and that people are fearing it, because it brings blood bonds with it and so the old want to avoid it feed from thin bloods or kill the cainite they are drinking from. But because it is not really a problem to those cainite couples who are blood bound to each other my question would be, would it possible for them, to embrace some of their servants so he drinks from mortals and so feed to his masters his vitae? Or would this not be possible because it is comming from generation and not from age?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the lack of humanity to consider in the factors. The more divorced you are from humanity as the centuries pass, the chances of you losing the taste for human blood, and needing something stronger to quell the hunger increases...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","user":"Gangrel44","date":". 06-25-2020, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T12:40:55-07:00","id":1398848,"title":"","content":"it's both generation and age<br /> <br /> methuselah's thirst is a plot device to force elders to embrace childer even when it's not in their best interest,<br /> it's thanks to it that you'll still see 5th gens popping up here and there seemingly out of nowhere,<br /> <br /> it's also one of the ways you can collect favors from elders,<br /> by...prostituting your blood? well, let's just call it offering them blood<br /> <br /> it's also a good way to survive as a thinblood<br /> <br /> you can easily bypass the bloodbond by feeding from different vampires each night (have more than one childe, MOAR 5TH GENS)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-25-2020, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T13:12:53-07:00","id":1398861,"title":"","content":"Low Generation, Elevated Age and low Humanity (or comparable Paths of Enlightenment) can cause the Thirst.<br /> <br /> I remember in Diablerie Mexico, that a Methuselah had devised a blood magic ritual to drop his bloodbound Childer from 5th to 13th Generation, because in this way they wouldn't go in Torpor and can keep drinking human blood, and he had them guard him for like... 800 years(?)<br /> Admittedly, it was early 2nd edition, so things may have changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T16:51:58-07:00","id":1398898,"title":"","content":"I agree with the others that it is a combination of potent Generation, very long age, and low Humanity. You could probably create some kind of mathematical formula between the three and find a threshold past which Methusaleh's Thirst is increasingly going to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T20:17:26-07:00","id":1398938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398800-methuselah-s-thirst-from-age-or-generation?p=1398898#post1398898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the others that it is a combination of potent Generation, very long age, and low Humanity. You could probably create some kind of mathematical formula between the three and find a threshold past which Methusaleh's Thirst is increasingly going to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>6th Generation and lower, 500+ years undead or more, Humanity or Path at 3 or lower. And all three factors must be met for the methuselah's thirst to take effect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","user":"Gangrel44","date":". 06-25-2020, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T20:44:05-07:00","id":1398941,"title":"","content":"In its discussion of elder characters the Dark Ages Storyteller Companion (WW 20003) it has a section on Methuselah's thirst. On pg 76 had an interesting list of potential triggers for Methuselah's Thirst in a sidebar as well as system rules for it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Character is a diablerist<br /> - Sire is addicted to Cainite vitae<br /> - Character's Road rating is 3 or less<br /> - Character follows the Roads of the Beast, Metamorphosis, or Blood<br /> - Character is active for 500 or more years<br /> - Character has a Derangement related to blood or feeding<br /> - Character has created five or more childer<br /> - Character has placed five or more Cainites under blood oath<br /> - Character has a Nature other than Architect, Caregiver, Cavalier or Martyr </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Storytellers who prefer a systematic approach should require players to make a Willpower roll for every few centuries of game time. The difficulty of the roll is the number of &quot;trigger conditions&quot; the character possesses, with a minimum of 2 (one trigger equals difficulty 2, seven triggers results in a a difficulty of 7). Success on the roll means that the character need not drink vampiric vitae (though she may choose to). Failure indicates the Cainite is wavering, experiencing a thirst for Cainite vitae and drinking it when the opportunity presents itself but not yet required to do so. Such characters must roll again after a period determined by the Storyteller (perhaps a few years within the chronic). If the roll fails again, the character must drink vampiric blood to survive. A botch at any point means the character can only draw nourishment from Cainite vitae. </div> </div> </div>Basically there was no one specific factor that caused a vampire to develop Methuselah's Thirst. Similarly a vampire might have a number of potential triggers but still be sated by lesser blood regardless. Essentially it's up to the ST to determine when/if that change occurs for a character.<br /> <br /> As for your second question, yes a vampire could embrace someone to feed on them if they could only drink Cainite vitae. However unless the vampire in question is already blood bound or participates in Vaulderie, they're going to need to worry about the blood oath. As for your blood couple, they'll likely end up in a situation where they're addicted to Cainite vitae. For them hunger frenzy could be extremely dangerous since their partner is likely to be the closest source of palatable blood.<br /> <br /> While I wouldn't normally mention it Requiem touched on a situation similar to this due to the Coils of Blood. Essentially there was a power that gave you an extra blood point for what you took. So two vampires with the power who fed off each other (thus each generating blood through the act) were called a Hungarian Marriage. It was described as a bad thing because they'd both be hopelessly blood addicted time bombs that are one frenzy away from disaster and a blood addled predator hunting their own kind. Larger groups end up in a daisy chain standoff where if one dies the link of blood bonds collapse and the hunger can easily lead to destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T03:38:51-07:00","id":1398999,"title":"","content":"Thank you Gangrel and Cynic. Your last posts here are very helpfull.<br /> And I think I will handle it myself, that Golconda even protects from and clears any existing Thirst of Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 06-26-2020, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T04:27:50-07:00","id":1399014,"title":"","content":"Tinfoil time: <br /> <br /> Methuselah's thirst is an idea concocted by Ancillae to cause neonates to be more against elders and to justify the idea that Gehenna will come and all the Old vampires will devour their children. Later on it was appropriated to be a warn people against diablerie. Methuselah's thirst is a myth, or perhaps, like vampires who fear crosses and running water, it is a myth that comes true through the power of belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T04:36:35-07:00","id":1399017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398800-methuselah-s-thirst-from-age-or-generation?p=1399014#post1399014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tinfoil time:</div> </div> </div> </div>careful, you're slowly becoming like Phipps<br /> keep your wild ideas in check -_-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T04:48:04-07:00","id":1399020,"title":"","content":"To my knowledge There is no concrete evidence that I am wrong. Methuselah's thirst has always been posited as a rumour or something some people suffer from but not others. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T05:07:53-07:00","id":1399026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398800-methuselah-s-thirst-from-age-or-generation?p=1399020#post1399020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my knowledge There is no concrete evidence that I am wrong. Methuselah's thirst has always been posited as a rumour or something some people suffer from but not others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T07:45:51-07:00","id":1399064,"title":"","content":"In V5, Tremeres are the best source of kindred blood! Little fear of being blood-bonded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T07:58:16-07:00","id":1399066,"title":"","content":"I have Helena stuck with it, and Mithras. I never use it beyond Helena when I'm running Chicago. In a way it makes it a flaw. I always thought of Helena's turn to murdering evil psycho to be more a product of how truly nasty Mino's was. Less learned behavior and more 30-40% of her personality is her warped sire changing her when she ate him.<br /> <br /> I am pretty sure Methuselah's Thirst is just another thing swiped from Anne Rice books. I think the idea is silly and personally don't bother with it in games. If Helena went to a Salubri abuse counselor and got back her humanity I'd let her survive on animal's if she wanted to. Kinda ends the point of Helena though if you reform her. Wouldn't she just peacefully wander off and live on a beach in Greece somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 06-26-2020, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T10:20:26-07:00","id":1399096,"title":"","content":"That said, I think the actual concept of Methuselah's Thirst is a bit abused.<br /> What is less noticeable about this phenomenon is not the &quot;Methuselah&quot;, but the &quot;Thirst&quot; part.<br /> Like, the Kindred afflicted by it doesn't become unable to drink kine's vitae, but from time to time is swiped by a raging craving for Kindred vitae.<br /> It's basically the same craving that a animals-drinking Kindred gets for human vitae.<br /> To make an example, Helena could hardly survive for long if she could drink only Kindred vitae. In Chicago there were roughly 200 Kindred in the best time (Chicago by Night 1st edition), if Helena was forced to drink only from them (and consequently kill the victim in fear of blood bound), she would off 3 or 4 Kindred each month, which means almost 50 Kindred in a year. There were Sabbat Crusades with a death toll inferior to this.<br /> <br /> So, my take in the matter is just that the Methuselah's Thirst makes you craving for Kindred blood at the point that the more you resist, the more it becomes unbearable (and, of course, is unbearable for a Methuselah just awakened from Torpor). But beside seeing the other vampires as walking Happy Meals, the Methuselah can still feed from kine. She just doesn't really enjoys it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T17:10:50-07:00","id":1399166,"title":"","content":"I always took it that the Thirst was not constant. So once you fed, you were satiated for a while - perhaps depending on how the generation of the vampire and how long the vampire had lived. That may last you a while before the Thirst again compels you to feed on another vampire. In the meantime, normal feeding was possible.<br /> <br /> As an ST, I would rule this would be something that accelerates over time - that the Methusaleh must feed again quicker and quicker. At the time of Gehenna, they'd be devouring their children left and right because that's what supposed to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T18:38:44-07:00","id":1399185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398800-methuselah-s-thirst-from-age-or-generation?p=1399064#post1399064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In V5, Tremeres are the best source of kindred blood! Little fear of being blood-bonded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. The new Tremere weakness in V5 is a ticking time bomb for Clan Tremere. Once the other clans' elders figure out what's going on, the Tremere might as well re-name themselves Clan Open Buffet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T01:56:25-07:00","id":1399230,"title":"","content":"To be fair if you were going to diablerise someone you'd only get a first point of a blood bond which is something you could easily dismiss. If anything, a sustainable Tremere farm might boost the power of the Tremere as ancients work to increase the numbers of Tremere and protect the ones around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T06:39:27-07:00","id":1399281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SalamanDer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398800-methuselah-s-thirst-from-age-or-generation?p=1399096#post1399096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make an example, Helena could hardly survive for long if she could drink only Kindred vitae. In Chicago there were roughly 200 Kindred in the best time (Chicago by Night 1st edition), if Helena was forced to drink only from them (and consequently kill the victim in fear of blood bound), she would off 3 or 4 Kindred each month, which means almost 50 Kindred in a year. There were Sabbat Crusades with a death toll inferior to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing says they have to be established kindred. Embrace someone or have someone else embrace them for you, (I think the V5 Chicago by Night establishes that Brett Striker is doing exactly that for her), feed a second mortal to them to fill up their blood, then you drain them. No fuss about blood bonds, no kindred is missing that anybody knows about.<br /> Lets go with your number of 4 times per month, thats 8 mortals missing, around 100 per year. If they're not targeting the upper 1% kids, they can likely get away with it, especially since the control the police and &quot;evidence that your kid ran away&quot; is easy to manufacture. For the mortal victim they can just fake gang related crimes etc.<br /> <br /> It's really not that hard for an elder to get away with this, at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}